        "payload": "tree caae0b50a3689c0e94521e0aba89852c07cc4c61\nparent cce32b16874e85e8a00cfa1a2190f0b6f4dcaf66\nauthor Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792102639 +0200\ncommitter Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792178574 +0200\n\ncrypto: cleanse CSHA512 state in its destructor\n\nFinalize() leaves the digest in the hasher's state, and the last block\nin its buffer. Every CSHA512 outside tests and benchmarks hashes secret\ndata: in BytesToKeySHA512AES the final state is the wallet encryption\nkey and IV, and the RNG hashers hold seed material.\n\nCleanse both in a destructor, as ChaCha20 does, so that each hasher is\nwiped when it goes out of scope instead of each caller cleansing it.\n",
