      "body": "Any motivation to this other than:\n > ...as src/bip324.cpp does for its hkdf object and as https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36537 proposes for the HMAC hashers.\n\nI can understand why it was done for `hkdf` , but are there any risks posed here? Even if there were, creating a destructor at the class level should be the way to go, imo; otherwise, we will be going into a cleaning spree for every finalized digest",
