      "body": "Agreed, done: CSHA512 now cleanses its state and buffer in its destructor, as ChaCha20 does, and the line in crypter.cpp is gone. The risk is small: after the function returns, the key and IV derived from the passphrase stay on the stack until overwritten, where a crash dump or another memory bug could expose them. Every CSHA512 outside tests and benchmarks hashes secret data, so the class is the right place for the wipe. This also covers the RNG hashers, so I'm closing #36551.\n",
